🪜 Line-by-Line Explanation
🔹 dfs1()

Standard DFS

Push node to stack after visiting neighbors

This ensures finish time order

🔹 Transpose Graph
transpose.get(nbr).add(i);


Reverse direction of every edge.

🔹 dfs2()

DFS on reversed graph

Each call prints one SCC

🔹 Stack Usage

Stack ensures we process nodes in correct order to isolate SCCs.

